  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Ma&#xdf;nahmen zur Unterst&#xfc;tzung des Umwelt- und Klimaschutzes und der Anpassung an den Klimawandel (FONERWA)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Measures to support environmental and climate change mitigation and adaptation (FONERWA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Die FZ-Ma&#xdf;nahme f&#xf6;rdert die Umsetzung von Umwelt und Klimaschutz- bzw. Klimaanpassungsma&#xdf;nahmen auf lokaler Ebene, &#xfc;ber den ruandischen Umwelt- und Klimafonds (Rwanda Green Fund - RGF). &#xdc;bergeordnetes Ziel des Vorhabens ist die Steigerung der Resilienz gegen&#xfc;ber den Auswirkungen des Klimawandels und die Sicherung der nachhaltigen sozio&#xf6;konomischen Entwicklung Ruandas. Zielgruppe des Vorhabens ist die gesamte Bev&#xf6;lkerung in den 30 Distrikten Ruandas, die von den Folgen des Klimawandels betroffen und von der nachhaltigen Nutzung der nat&#xfc;rlichen Ressourcen abh&#xe4;ngig istDas Vorhaben besteht aus drei Komponenten:- Komponente 1 - (Klimaschutzprojekte in den Distrikten) wurden Einzelvorhaben auf Basis von Projektantr&#xe4;gen der Distrikte ausgew&#xe4;hlt und umgesetzt, so z.B. die Ausweitung eines Entw&#xe4;sserungskanals und die Vergr&#xf6;&#xdf;erung von Br&#xfc;cken in der Industriezone Nyabugogo/Kigali.- Komponente 2 - Erstellung ausschreibungsreifer Planungsunterlagen des Green City Kigali Pilotareals- Komponente 3 - mit SIDA und FCDO kofinanzierter Consultingauftrag zur institutionellen Beratung des Rwanda Green Fund</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The FC measure promotes the implementation of environmental and climate protection and adaptation measures at the local level through the Rwandan environment and climate fund (Rwanda Green Fund - RGF). The overall objective of the project is to increase resilience to the impacts of climate change and to ensure sustainable socio-economic development in Rwanda. The target group of the project is the entire population in the 30 districts of Rwanda, which is affected by the consequences of climate change and dependent on the sustainable use of natural resources.The project consists of three components:- Component 1 - (climate protection projects in the districts), individual projects were selected and implemented on the basis of project applications from the districts, such as the expansion of a drainage canal and the enlargement of bridges in the Nyabugogo/Kigali industrial zone.- Component 2 - Preparation of tender-ready planning documents for the Green City Kigali pilot site- Component 3 - Consulting contract co-financed with SIDA and FCDO to provide institutional support to the Rwanda Green Fund</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">F&#xf6;rderung lokaler Klimaanpassungsma&#xdf;nahmen auf der Basis von Einzelprojektantr&#xe4;gen &#xfc;ber den nationalen Fond f&#xfc;r Umwelt und Klima in Ruanda (FONERWA)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The FC measure promotes the implementation of environmental and climate protection and adaptation measures at the local level through the Rwandan environment and climate fund (Rwanda Green Fund - RGF). The overall objective of the project is to increase resilience to the impacts of climate change and to ensure sustainable socio-economic development in Rwanda. The target group of the project is the entire population in the 30 districts of Rwanda, which is affected by the consequences of climate change and dependent on the sustainable use of natural resources.The project consists of three components:- Component 1 - (climate protection projects in the districts), individual projects were selected and implemented on the basis of project applications from the districts, such as the expansion of a drainage canal and the enlargement of bridges in the Nyabugogo/Kigali industrial zone.- Component 2 - Preparation of tender-ready planning documents for the Green City Kigali pilot site- Component 3 - Consulting contract co-financed with SIDA and FCDO to provide institutional support to the Rwanda Green Fund</narrative>
  </description>
